quran[16]{c,v,t}:
  43,74,"Indeed, the guilty will remain forever in the punishment of Hell."
  43,75,"It will not be lightened for them, and they will be overwhelmed in utter despair."
  43,76,"We did not wrong them, but they were the wrongdoers themselves."
  43,77,"They will call out (to the guard of Hell): ‘O Malik! Let your Lord bring an end to us!’ He will say: ‘Indeed, you will stay on (forever).’"
  43,78,"We certainly brought you the truth, but most of you were resentful of the truth."
  43,79,"Have they devised any (evil) plan? Indeed, We (too) are surely planning."
  43,80,"Do they think We do not hear their hidden thoughts and their secret talks? Yes, We do! And Our messenger angels are with them, writing (everything) down."
  43,81,"Say: ‘If (supposing the impossible that) the Most-Compassionate (Lord) had a son, I would be the first to worship (him).’"
  43,82,"Glorified is the Lord of the heavens and the earth, the Lord of the Throne, far above what they claim (about Him)!"
  43,83,So leave them to gossip and play until they encounter their Day which they have been promised.
  43,84,"It is He Who is (the only) God in the heavens and (the only) God on the earth. And He is the All-Wise, the All-Knowing."
  43,85,"Blessed is He, to Whom the kingdom of the heavens and the earth belongs and whatsoever is between them. And with Him lies the knowledge of the Hour. And to Him, you will be returned."
  43,86,"Those (idols) they worship besides Him have no power of intercession, except those who testify to the truth and know (for whom to intercede)."
  43,87,(Esteemed Prophet!) If you ask them: ‘Who created them?’ They will certainly say: ‘Allah.’ How are they then deluded (from the truth)?
  43,88,"By the Messenger’s words: ‘O my Lord! Indeed, these are the people who do not believe!’"
  43,89,So bear with them and say: ‘Peace!’ They will soon come to know (their end).
